Relation to upstream

training/veomni/, training/tasks/train_torch.py and
training/configs/pretrain/qwen2_5_coder_500M.yaml are identical to Open-dLLM at
commit 5b9ba4d (github.com/pengzhangzhi/Open-dLLM) except for the nine files
below. The complete difference is in PATCH_vs_Open-dLLM-5b9ba4d.diff; applying
it to Open-dLLM@5b9ba4d reproduces this snapshot exactly.

Modifications by the CDLM authors (absorbing + uniform mixture corruption
objective and supporting changes):

  veomni/data/data_collator.py
      DataCollatorWithPositionIDsMixture_Masking: after absorbing (mask)
      corruption, replaces a fraction mixture_prob of the still-visible tokens
      with uniformly sampled tokens and keeps supervision on masked and
      corrupted positions.
  veomni/data/data_loader.py
      Selects the mixture collator when mixture_prob > 0.
  veomni/utils/arguments.py
      mixture_prob, noise_token_wt, clean_token_wt, eval_before_train,
      eval_batch_size.
  veomni/models/transformers/qwen2/modeling_qwen2.py
  veomni/models/transformers/qwen3/modeling_qwen3.py
      Weighted cross-entropy on corrupted (noise_token_wt) and clean
      (clean_token_wt) visible tokens; confidence logging.
  veomni/distributed/parallel_state.py
  veomni/distributed/sequence_parallel/comm.py
      45-minute process-group timeouts.
  tasks/train_torch.py
      Wiring of the mixture arguments, evaluation before training,
      refactored HumanEval hook.

Upstream change not included:

  veomni/models/module_utils.py
      This snapshot predates an upstream fix (Open-dLLM 243b97e, which adds a
      missing `from functools import partial` import). The file is kept as it
      was when the paper's checkpoints were trained.

Provenance of the released checkpoints

  CDLM-0.5B (Hugging Face Shuibai12138/CDLM-0.5B, also published as
  Shuibai12138/Open-Dcoder-0.5B-mixture-mdm-step2000):
      step 2000 of run Open-Dcoder-0.5B-continue-mixture-mdm-20251115-115315
  MDLM-0.5B baseline (Shuibai12138/Open-Dcoder-0.5B-baseline-mdm-step2000):
      step 2000 of run
      Baseline-Open-Dcoder-0.5B-continue-mixture-mdm-20251115-220242

  Both runs: seed 42, 4 x A100-PCIE-40GB, global batch 12, Python 3.11.13,
  torch 2.5.0 (CUDA 12.4 build), transformers 4.54.1, tokenizers 0.21.4,
  datasets 3.6.0, every other package at the version pinned in
  requirements.txt. Code: the development repository this snapshot was
  taken from, at commit 409879f. The full resolved configurations are
  configs/cdlm/headline_resolved.yaml and
  configs/cdlm/headline_mdlm_resolved.yaml; they differ only in
  mixture_prob, noise_token_wt and the run names.

  veomni/, tasks/train_torch.py and configs/pretrain/ in this directory are
  that repository at the later commit 4c13f87, which the multi-seed runs
  (seeds 1234 and 2025) and the clean-token-weight run used, with
  transformers 4.57.0, tokenizers 0.22.2 and datasets 4.2.0 (the pins in
  requirements.txt). From 409879f to 4c13f87 four files change; none of
  the changes affects the data, the loss or the gradients:

  tasks/train_torch.py
      The HF export written at an evaluation step goes to
      hf_ckpt_step_<step> instead of hf_ckpt (output path). NCCL_TIMEOUT
      defaults to 3600 before the process group is created (timeout).
  veomni/distributed/parallel_state.py
      Comments and an unused local variable.
  veomni/distributed/sequence_parallel/comm.py
      45-minute timeout on the sequence- and context-parallel process
      groups (timeout).
  veomni/models/transformers/qwen2/modeling_qwen2.py
      The logged ratio conf_ratio = clean_conf / noise_conf is clamped at
      10000 instead of 100. It is computed under no_grad and only logged,
      so the headline runs' logged conf_ratio is capped at 100.

  How this was established. The published weights were loaded into this
  code, in the requirements.txt environment, and trained with lr = 1e-30
  (weights effectively frozen) on the headline data stream. For both runs
  the loss at step 2001, computed from the published weights, is bitwise
  equal to the loss the original run logged at step 2001 from its own
  step-2000 weights, and so is every logged loss component (for CDLM apart
  from the conf_ratio clamp above). This identifies the published
  weights and shows that data order and corruption noise match for 2001
  steps. A fresh MDLM run with scripts/train_0.5b.sh also reproduces the
  recorded losses of steps 1 and 2 bitwise.

